Description: fdrv/bsp: limit confirmation copy to the caller's cfm buffer size
 cmd_mgr_msgind() copied the firmware-reported param_len (capped only at
 RWNX_CMD_E2AMSG_LEN_MAX) into the caller's cfm buffer, which is often a
 much smaller stack struct. Record sizeof(*cfm) in struct rwnx_cmd when
 the command is sent (rwnx_send_msg/rwnx_send_msg1 become wrapper
 macros, no call sites change) and copy at most that many bytes,
 warning on truncation.
 .
 The variable-length DBG_CUSTOM_MSG_CFM (CONFIG_MCU_MESSAGE) is the one
 exception: rwnx_send_dbg_custom_msg_req() now takes the size of the
 caller's allocation and passes it as the copy limit, and
 handle_custom_msg() sizes that allocation from max_bytes_to_read and
 caps the firmware-reported cfm->len at it before copying out.
Author: N Oliver <3945917+PixnBits@users.noreply.github.com>
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-26
